,"context":"(4) While nameplate at the LMD Bitcoin Mining Facilities was 10.9 EH/s and 9.7 EH/s as of December 31, 2025 and 2024, respectively, actual operational hashrate depends on a variety of factors, including (but not limited to) performance tuning to increase efficiency and maximize margin, scheduled outages (scopes to improve reliability or performance), unscheduled outages, curtailment due to participation in various cash generating demand response programs, derate of ASICS due to adverse weather and ASIC maintenance and repair.","section":"ITEM 7. Management’s Discussion and Analysis of Financial Condition and Results of Operations","block":492,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001083301-26-000031","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-27","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001083301","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1083301/000108330126000031/wulf-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/e42ae32f2a5a9f82463bb4a84068ea06ef0936c625ca70fb3f7c19ef0758845f.bin","sha256":"e42ae32f2a5a9f82463bb4a84068ea06ef0936c625ca70fb3f7c19ef0758845f"}},{"id":"bb7a48030fdf6b4ee723890760d0c463709f6c13159b4adfc7898b8fbf26943d","quote":"The table below presents the average cost of mining each bitcoin, including bitcoin mined at the LMD Bitcoin Mining Facilities and the Company’s net share of bitcoin mined at the Nautilus Cryptomine Facility, for the years ended December 31, 2025 and 2024 and the total energy cost per kWh utilized within the facilities.","context":"Bitcoin Mining - Average Cost of Bitcoin Mined","section":"ITEM 7. Management’s Discussion and Analysis of Financial Condition and Results of Operations","block":496,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001083301-26-000031","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-27","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001083301","url":"https://www.sec.go